            <ArticleTitle>[Intravenous theophylline therapy. Effect of solubilizers on the incidence of adverse local effects in the area of infusion?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>643-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The frequency and intensity of discomfort and pain at the site of injection during intravenous infusion of theophylline sodium glycinate and theophylline ethylenediamine were compared in a single blind crossover study on 6 healthy adult volunteers. The preparation containing theophylline sodium glycinate was significantly better tolerated than theophylline ethylenediamine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
